Let us consider our quadruple <img alt="$(a,b,c,d)$" class="latex" height="20" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/faedb9d30dc3763d92cbcacf2cc17e2bf64f3e8b.png" style="vertical-align: -5px" width="75"/> as the following image <img alt="$xaxbcxxdxx$" class="latex" height="12" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b12d3e3cc0a221112fc4ce90d2c2c1e03cc611.png" width="97"/>. The location of the letter <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/>, <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/>, <img alt="$c$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/>, <img alt="$d$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> represents its value and <img alt="$x$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="12"/> is a place holder. Clearly the quadruple is interesting if there are more place holders between <img alt="$c$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> and <img alt="$d$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> than there are between <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> and <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/>. 
<img alt="$0$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> holders between <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> and <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> means we consider <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> and <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> as one unit <img alt="$ab$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="19"/> and <img alt="$c$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> as <img alt="$cx$" class="latex" height="8" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cf0656f4a0f22578337c8747d8cf77966350d6d.png" width="18"/> yielding <img alt="$\binom83 = 56$" class="latex" height="53" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/7611fb2b6aa5cf8f46fbdc50ed1ad96eadbb2b3a.png" style="vertical-align: -22px" width="79"/> ways; 
<img alt="$1$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> holder between <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> and <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> means we consider <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> and <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> as one unit <img alt="$axb$" class="latex" height="12" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd3aa3c32753e5e6d41456ccc671c07481a0037.png" width="28"/> and <img alt="$c$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> as <img alt="$cxx$" class="latex" height="8" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e01e885cb8fc508809808c3203af4765fa5a89b.png" width="28"/> yielding <img alt="$\binom 63 = 20$" class="latex" height="53" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/671823a8c9921757ffec71a1531813f0273ac4bf.png" style="vertical-align: -22px" width="79"/> ways; 
<img alt="$2$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> holders between <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> and <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> means we consider <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> and <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> as one unit <img alt="$axxb$" class="latex" height="12" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c6a0b6984e916e990611860c448ee0d901af88.png" width="38"/> and <img alt="$c$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> as <img alt="$cxxx$" class="latex" height="8" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350dd27a2afd51c0e1f966d0830992392223434b.png" width="39"/> yielding <img alt="$\binom43 = 4$" class="latex" height="53" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc819c7a43258aa242996092754e6fe2fc557e50.png" style="vertical-align: -22px" width="70"/> ways.
Since there cannot be <img alt="$3$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> holders between <img alt="$a$" class="latex" height="10" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="11"/> and <img alt="$b$" class="latex" height="14" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png" style="vertical-align: -1px" width="10"/> so our total is <img alt="$56+20+4=\fbox{080}$" class="latex" height="24" src="//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7c6647ac8d247e8db5b1b888aae9a25fb9abe2.png" style="vertical-align: -6px" width="152"/>.
